# Profile Feature - Frontend Rules

## Architecture Principles

### Monolith by Features
- All profile-related code in `lib/features/profile/`
- Structure: models/, services/, bloc/, pages/, widgets/
- Feature-specific widgets in widgets/, shared widgets in lib/core/widgets/

### Feature Separation
- **Profile handles**: User profiles, posts CRUD, user stats, profile display
- **Social handles**: Comments, likes, saves, comment replies
- Profile USES social widgets (CommentCard, CommentInputField) - don't duplicate
- Keep feature boundaries clear

## Code Organization

### Directory Structure
```
lib/features/profile/
├── models/           # PostModel, UserModel, StatsModel
├── services/         # PostService, PostRepository
├── bloc/             # UserPostsCubit, UserPostsState
├── pages/            # ProfilePage, PostDetailPage, SavedPostsPage
├── widgets/          # ProfileHeader, ProfileStats, PostCard
├── posts/widgets/    # Post-specific widgets
└── profile_routes.dart
```

### Model Layer
- All models must extend Equatable for value comparison
- Include fromJson/toJson for API serialization
- Use copyWith for immutable updates
- Example:
```dart
class PostModel extends Equatable {
  final String id;
  final bool isLikedByCurrentUser;
  final bool isSavedByCurrentUser;

  // NEVER use default values for interaction fields
  // Backend always sends them (no omitempty)

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [id, isLikedByCurrentUser, ...];

  PostModel copyWith({bool? isLikedByCurrentUser, ...}) { ... }
}
```

### Service Layer
- Repository handles API calls via ApiService.useFetch
- Service adds business logic on top of repository
- Use BaseRepository methods: fetchPaginatedList, create, update, delete
- Example:
```dart
class PostRepository extends BaseRepository<PostModel> {
  PostRepository() : super(endpoint: '/posts', fromJson: PostModel.fromJson);

  Future<Map<String, dynamic>> getUserPostsPaginated(String userId, {int page = 1}) async {
    return fetchPaginatedList(
      path: '/users/$userId/posts',
      queryParameters: {'page': page, 'limit': 20},
    );
  }
}
```

### BLoC Layer (Cubit Pattern)
- Use Cubit (not Bloc) for simpler state management
- States must be immutable and extend Equatable
- Emit new instances for every state change
- Handle optimistic updates with error rollback

## State Management

### User Posts Cubit
```dart
class UserPostsCubit extends Cubit<UserPostsState> {
  final PostService _postService;

  // Optimistic updates for interactions
  Future<void> toggleLike(String postId) async {
    final currentState = state;
    if (currentState is! UserPostsLoaded) return;

    // 1. Find post
    final index = currentState.posts.indexWhere((p) => p.id == postId);
    if (index == -1) return;

    final post = currentState.posts[index];
    final isLiked = post.isLikedByCurrentUser;

    // 2. Optimistic update
    final updatedPost = post.copyWith(
      likesCount: isLiked ? post.likesCount - 1 : post.likesCount + 1,
      isLikedByCurrentUser: !isLiked,
    );

    // IMPORTANT: Use typed List.from
    final updatedPosts = List<PostModel>.from(currentState.posts);
    updatedPosts[index] = updatedPost;
    emit(currentState.copyWith(posts: updatedPosts));

    // 3. Real API call
    try {
      if (isLiked) {
        await _postService.unlikePost(postId);
      } else {
        await _postService.likePost(postId);
      }
    } catch (e) {
      // 4. Revert on error
      emit(currentState);
    }
  }
}
```

### State Classes
```dart
abstract class UserPostsState extends Equatable {
  const UserPostsState();
  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [];
}

class UserPostsLoaded extends UserPostsState {
  final List<PostModel> posts;
  final bool hasMore;
  final int currentPage;

  const UserPostsLoaded({
    required this.posts,
    this.hasMore = false,
    this.currentPage = 1,
  });

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [posts, hasMore, currentPage];

  // copyWith for immutable updates
  UserPostsLoaded copyWith({List<PostModel>? posts, bool? hasMore, int? currentPage}) {
    return UserPostsLoaded(
      posts: posts ?? this.posts,
      hasMore: hasMore ?? this.hasMore,
      currentPage: currentPage ?? this.currentPage,
    );
  }
}
```

## UI Components

### Using Social Components
```dart
// ✅ DO: Use social components for comments
import '../../social/comment/comment_card.dart';
import '../../social/comment/comment_input_field.dart';
import '../../social/comment/comments_cubit.dart';

// In PostDetailPage
BlocProvider(
  create: (_) => getIt<CommentsCubit>()..fetchComments(postId),
  child: Column(children: [
    BlocBuilder<CommentsCubit, CommentsState>(
      builder: (context, state) {
        if (state is CommentsLoaded) {
          return ListView.builder(
            itemCount: state.comments.length,
            itemBuilder: (context, index) {
              return CommentCard(
                comment: state.comments[index],
                onLike: () => context.read<CommentsCubit>().toggleLike(comment.id),
                onReply: () => _handleReply(comment),
              );
            },
          );
        }
      },
    ),
    CommentInputField(onSubmit: (text) => _submitComment(text)),
  ]),
)

// ❌ DON'T: Create duplicate comment widgets in profile
```

