## Navigation

### Route Management
```dart
// Define routes in profile_routes.dart
class ProfileRoutes {
  static const String profile = '/profile';
  static const String postDetail = '/profile/posts/:id';
  static const String postCreate = '/profile/posts/create';
  static const String savedPosts = '/profile/saved';
  static const String editProfile = '/profile/edit';

  static String getPostDetail(String postId) => '/profile/posts/$postId';
  static String getUserProfile(String userId) => '/users/$userId';
}
```

### Navigation Best Practices
```dart
// ✅ DO: Use context.push() to maintain stack
onTap: () => context.push(ProfileRoutes.getPostDetail(post.id))

// ❌ DON'T: Use NavigationService().go() - replaces stack
onTap: () => NavigationService().go(context, route)  // BAD

// For going back
onBackPressed: () => context.pop()
```

## API Integration

### Pagination Response Structure
```dart
// Backend sends: {status, message, data: {data: [...], pagination: {...}}}
Future<Map<String, dynamic>> getPostCommentsPaginated(String postId, {int page = 1}) async {
  final response = await useFetch(/* ... */);

  if (response.status == 'success' && response.data != null) {
    final responseData = response.data as Map<String, dynamic>;

    // IMPORTANT: Backend uses 'data' not 'items'
    final items = (responseData['data'] as List<dynamic>)
        .map((e) => Comment.fromJson(e))
        .toList();

    final pagination = responseData['pagination'] as Map<String, dynamic>;

    return {
      'items': items,
      'currentPage': pagination['currentPage'],
      'totalPages': pagination['totalPages'],
      'totalItems': pagination['totalItems'],
      'hasNextPage': pagination['hasNext'],  // Note: 'hasNext' not 'hasNextPage'
      'hasPreviousPage': pagination['hasPrevious'],
    };
  }
  throw Exception('Failed to fetch comments');
}
```

### Error Handling
```dart
try {
  final response = await _postService.createPost(post);
  if (mounted) {
    context.push(ProfileRoutes.getPostDetail(response.id));
  }
} catch (e) {
  if (mounted) {
    ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(
      SnackBar(content: Text(context.tr('error.creating.post'))),
    );
  }
}
```

## Common Pitfalls

### ❌ DON'T
- Use List.from() without type parameter - causes type errors
- Use default values for isLikedByCurrentUser - backend always sends it
- Duplicate comment widgets - use social feature components
- Use NavigationService().go() from profile - breaks navigation stack
- Forget to check `mounted` before showing dialogs/snackbars
- Use debugPrint in production code - use AppLogger instead

### ✅ DO
- Use List<PostModel>.from() with explicit type
- Trust backend to always send interaction fields
- Import and use social widgets for comments
- Use context.push() for navigation within profile
- Check `if (mounted)` before async UI operations
- Use AppLogger.debug/info/error for logging

## Dependency Injection

### Service Registration
```dart
// In lib/core/di/injection.dart
void setupProfileDependencies() {
  // Repositories
  getIt.registerLazySingleton(() => PostRepository());
  getIt.registerLazySingleton(() => UserRepository());

  // Services
  getIt.registerLazySingleton(() => PostService(getIt()));

  // Cubits (Factories - new instance each time)
  getIt.registerFactory(() => UserPostsCubit(getIt()));
}
```

### Usage in Widgets
```dart
// In StatefulWidget
late UserPostsCubit _userPostsCubit;

@override
void initState() {
  super.initState();
  _userPostsCubit = getIt<UserPostsCubit>();
  _userPostsCubit.fetchUserPosts(userId);
}

@override
void dispose() {
  _userPostsCubit.close();  // Important: clean up
  super.dispose();
}

// Provide to widget tree
BlocProvider.value(
  value: _userPostsCubit,
  child: /* ... */,
)
```

